[[6122,2320,"During the course of Mr [name redacted] in-patient admission from the 13\" of May 2013 to the 13\" of August 2013, staff did not follow the requirements of the Trust' Prevention and Management of Pressure Ulcers Policy in that incident reports were not submitted.","pressure ulcer development",""],[6123,2320,"Due to the co-morbidities of Mr Hudson, he ought to have been identified as having a higher risk factor.","risk factor identification",""],[6124,2320,"Mr Hudson ought to have been referred to the foot protection team in a more timely manner.","delayed foot protection referral",""],[6125,2320,"The nursing documentation was not as comprehensive as it ought to have been.","incomplete nursing documentation",""],[6126,2320,"The classification of Mr [name redacted] heel injuries was","inconsistent injury classification",""],[6127,2320,"there were episodes of inadequate record keeping; for example, although the family had met with medical staff to discuss concerns, there appeared to be no available record or the action taken thereafter; also Mr Hudson was to have the benefit of an Exogen machine for 20 minutes each day to stimulate the healing of the bone, but there appeared to be no records about this;","inadequate record keeping",""],[6504,2477,"There was a failure to give Mr Dixon an appointment 6 months after he was seen in August 2012","delayed follow up appointment",""],[6505,2477,"There was a failure to give Mr Dixon an urgent appointment for a procedure within 4-6 weeks of the 14/08/2013","missed urgent procedure",""],[6506,2477,"Important documentation was missing namely the referral form for the procedure that Civic Centre, Burdon Road","missing referral documentation",""],[6507,2477,"There appeared to be no systems in place to identify and take action to rectify these problems","lack of monitoring systems",""],[7765,2976,"The time taken to complete the initial documentation was longer than it ought to have been given the interruptions to the process.","delayed initial documentation",""],[7766,2976,"The omission to prescribe prophylactic Dalteparin had not been subject to any effective review by a clinician or a nurse.","failure to review prescription omission",""],[7767,2976,"When the pharmacy raised a query, it was not communicated effectively.","ineffective communication of pharmacy query",""],[7768,2976,"Systems, forms, checklists, policies, procedures and protocols and compliance with them may not be sufficiently robust to deal with human factors.","insufficiently robust systems and protocols",""],[7769,2976,"The failures prevailed without correction from 24 December until Mrs James' acute deterioration and death on 8 January 2014.","unaddressed systemic failures",""],[14207,5540,"Although the Splenomegaly (identified in Sunderland Royal Hospital on 16\" October 2016) would not have led to any changes in the management of Mr Vinson, I was concerned to hear in evidence, that Mr Vinson was meant to be under close supervision in his hospital room, but this was not the case despite a review of the falls risk assessment","lack of close supervision of patient at risk of falls",""],[14577,5697,"Evidence was given at the Inquest that there was no policy in place between City Hospitals Sunderland NHS Foundation Trust and County Durham and Darlington NHS Foundation Trust clarifying the areas of responsibility and channels of communication between the two when patients are referred.","lack of policy clarifying responsibility and communication",""],[14578,5697,"Evidence was given that there were poor levels of communication both direct and indirect between medical professionals at each trust and poor understanding of each other's differing practices and procedures.","poor communication and understanding between trusts",""]]